# AN OMITTED NULLABLE SLOT IS `null` (LGRA.13.11, LNUL.11.1).
#
# `make` emits a Knob giving only its key. Its three nullable slots, a
# String?, a Bool? and a Float?, take `null`, which the compiler writes into
# the emit as the fill. `seen` matches only if all three are null.
#
# This pins PARITY: both runtimes load the same artefact, so it holds that
# each reads the compiler's `null` fill as `null`. That the fill is `null` at
# all, rather than the zero of the slot's type, is pinned against the spec by
# pyds's test_omitted_slot_defaults.
assert Seed go=1
pump
